WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.734 --> 00:00:02.300
-Macklemore!

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:03.701
Welcome back to the show.

00:00:03.701 --> 00:00:04.767
Looking good, bud.

00:00:04.767 --> 00:00:05.968
I like
that double-breasted suit.

00:00:05.968 --> 00:00:07.434
-Thank you.
You know?

00:00:07.434 --> 00:00:08.934
-Yeah.
You look great, pal.

00:00:08.934 --> 00:00:10.334
-You know what?
I feel great,

00:00:10.334 --> 00:00:12.367
and before --
And I appreciate that.

00:00:12.367 --> 00:00:15.267
And before we start,
I just want to say

00:00:15.267 --> 00:00:17.400
the suit is Gucci.
Um...

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.100
-No, no, no, you don't have
to say that stuff.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:21.334
-But -- But -- But

00:00:21.334 --> 00:00:23.000
the suit is Gucci...
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.133
-...but the socks...

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:27.300
are Nike Dri-FIT.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:29.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:29.133 --> 00:00:31.000
You know what I'm saying?
-Wow.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.601
See, he knows how to do it.

00:00:32.601 --> 00:00:33.601
See, that's what
I'm talking about.

00:00:33.601 --> 00:00:35.701
Dri-FIT.
You need the Dri-FIT.

00:00:35.701 --> 00:00:38.534
You're getting sporty,
by the way.

00:00:38.534 --> 00:00:39.801
-I am.
-You really are.

00:00:39.801 --> 00:00:42.100
You're getting into golf.
-Yes, yes.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.601
-And how long
have you been into golf?

00:00:44.601 --> 00:00:45.667
-Four years?
-Yeah.

00:00:45.667 --> 00:00:47.167
-Yeah.
-Are you getting better?

00:00:47.167 --> 00:00:49.901
-No, worse, worse.
Way worse.

00:00:49.901 --> 00:00:51.801
I was good a year and a half in.

00:00:51.801 --> 00:00:53.300
Trajectory, pro.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:55.434
Now -- trash.

00:00:55.434 --> 00:00:57.801
-But what --
what happened to you?

00:00:57.801 --> 00:00:59.367
-Thinking.
Thinking.

00:00:59.367 --> 00:01:00.567
-Yeah, you're just overthinking?

00:01:00.567 --> 00:01:01.868
-Well, you know what?

00:01:01.868 --> 00:01:03.133
At a certain point, I was like,
"You know what?

00:01:03.133 --> 00:01:05.067
I should probably
finish the album.

00:01:05.067 --> 00:01:06.767
I should stop playing golf.

00:01:06.767 --> 00:01:09.934
I make money doing this,
and I lose money doing this."

00:01:09.934 --> 00:01:10.934
-Yeah, okay.
Yeah, interesting.

00:01:10.934 --> 00:01:12.934
-"Let's focus on the music."

00:01:12.934 --> 00:01:15.334
And then I stopped playing,
and then you are

00:01:15.334 --> 00:01:17.234
only on Instagram,
looking at other people

00:01:17.234 --> 00:01:18.634
telling you how to play golf,

00:01:18.634 --> 00:01:21.200
and you lose
all athletic ability.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.400
-You were at the --
-Oh, no.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:25.167
-The Pro-Am.
No, this is good.

00:01:25.167 --> 00:01:26.734
Look at this swing.
Look at that.

00:01:26.734 --> 00:01:28.567
That's a good-looking golfer.

00:01:28.567 --> 00:01:31.033
[ Applause ]

00:01:31.033 --> 00:01:32.067
Is this your --

00:01:32.067 --> 00:01:34.000
By the way,
is this your clothing?

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:36.400
-Yes, Bogey Boys.
So we started Bogey Boys.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:40.667
Golf brand -- hat, jacket,
shirt, pants, everything.

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:44.767
The sunglasses are Oakley,
and they are just there

00:01:44.767 --> 00:01:47.133
to prevent anyone
from seeing the tears.

00:01:47.133 --> 00:01:48.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.334 --> 00:01:49.934
-No, that's not true.
That is a great swing.

00:01:49.934 --> 00:01:51.801
I like -- see, what I do is,
when I play golf,

00:01:51.801 --> 00:01:54.067
I hold that for too long.
-Mm.

00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:55.868
-So even if your shot's bad,
you just go like -- ffw!

00:01:55.868 --> 00:01:57.701
-Yeah, they don't know.
-You just hold it and you go...

00:01:57.701 --> 00:01:59.734
-They can't tell on TV.
-No, yeah, it looks good.

00:01:59.734 --> 00:02:01.033
But then,
I got another photo of --

00:02:01.033 --> 00:02:03.667
Here's you. This is you
looking for your ball.

00:02:03.667 --> 00:02:04.834
-Yeah. No, no, no.
-I just thought that was funny.

00:02:04.834 --> 00:02:06.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.267 --> 00:02:08.701
That's why I had to -- equal.
I gotta show both pictures.

00:02:08.701 --> 00:02:12.067
-You know, it was the 18th hole
on the last day on Sunday...

00:02:12.067 --> 00:02:13.200
-Yeah.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:15.200
-...when I hit two people,
back-to-back.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:16.968
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.968 --> 00:02:19.267
Then I really had a long,
hard talk with myself

00:02:19.267 --> 00:02:22.400
later that night of, "Maybe this
is not the sport for you."

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:24.467
-Yeah, no, this is the sport
for you right here.

00:02:24.467 --> 00:02:25.501
-Yes.
-We love you.

00:02:25.501 --> 00:02:27.067
We love your music.
Congratulations.

00:02:27.067 --> 00:02:28.567
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:02:28.567 --> 00:02:32.267
-This Friday --
This Friday it comes out.

00:02:32.267 --> 00:02:33.467
You were working on the album.

00:02:33.467 --> 00:02:35.100
You had a tour all set up,

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:36.667
and then,
everything just changed.

00:02:36.667 --> 00:02:37.734
-Yeah.

00:02:37.734 --> 00:02:38.934
-Can you talk about that
a little bit?

00:02:38.934 --> 00:02:40.067
-Yes, COVID happened.

00:02:40.067 --> 00:02:43.634
And like everybody,
my world stopped.

00:02:43.634 --> 00:02:47.334
And, you know, for those of you
that might not follow my story,

00:02:47.334 --> 00:02:50.934
I am a recovering addict,
alcoholic,

00:02:50.934 --> 00:02:53.567
and have been
for the last 14 years.

00:02:53.567 --> 00:02:54.868
And COVID happens --
[ Applause ]

00:02:54.868 --> 00:02:57.067
Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:57.067 --> 00:02:58.300
Thank you.

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:01.367
And a big part of
my recovery community

00:03:01.367 --> 00:03:03.534
is going to physical
12-step meetings.

00:03:03.534 --> 00:03:07.167
And once those stopped,
I was alone,

00:03:07.167 --> 00:03:10.901
and the disease of addiction
was like, "Yo, this is crazy.

00:03:10.901 --> 00:03:14.033
The world has stopped.
You can get high."

00:03:14.033 --> 00:03:16.434
And eventually, I, um...

00:03:16.434 --> 00:03:20.734
I stopped doing the things that
prevented me from getting high,

00:03:20.734 --> 00:03:23.167
and I listened to that voice.

00:03:23.167 --> 00:03:27.501
And it was a couple weeks
of a relapse and very painful.

00:03:27.501 --> 00:03:30.801
And still working
on trust issues with myself

00:03:30.801 --> 00:03:33.400
and within my, you know,
close circle of friends.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:38.033
But it definitely was a reminder
that whatever I put

00:03:38.033 --> 00:03:41.501
in front of my recovery will be
the first thing that I lose.

00:03:41.501 --> 00:03:42.834
-Yeah.
Oh, my gosh.

00:03:42.834 --> 00:03:45.167
I'm so happy that you stopped...

00:03:45.167 --> 00:03:47.400
-Yeah.
-...and got to get help again.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:50.567
-Yeah. I think, for me,
it's not, like --

00:03:50.567 --> 00:03:52.200
It's not a linear path, right?
It's not like,

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:54.000
oh, once I realized
that I had --

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:57.100
It's one disease that tells you,
"You don't have a disease."

00:03:57.100 --> 00:04:00.734
-Wow.
-And I am doing my best,

00:04:00.734 --> 00:04:02.501
and I'm making mistakes.

00:04:02.501 --> 00:04:05.200
And there's some in the future,
too, somewhere along the line,

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:07.133
in some capacity to my life,
but I want to be able

00:04:07.133 --> 00:04:10.267
to share that with the people
that I love and that follow me.

00:04:10.267 --> 00:04:12.033
-I appreciate the honesty.
-Yeah.

00:04:12.033 --> 00:04:13.801
-We love you.
-Yeah. I love you, buddy.

00:04:13.801 --> 00:04:15.701
-We love you.
-Yeah.

00:04:15.701 --> 00:04:17.701
-Does that --

00:04:17.701 --> 00:04:20.801
It's scary because, yeah,
I do want to say it again --

00:04:20.801 --> 00:04:21.934
we love you.
-Yeah.

00:04:21.934 --> 00:04:24.033
-I really love you so much.
-Thank you.

00:04:24.033 --> 00:04:25.501
Thank you.
I feel the same way.

00:04:25.501 --> 00:04:26.968
[ Cheers and applause ]
-You've been great to us.

00:04:26.968 --> 00:04:30.167
I've known you for --
I've known you for a decade.

00:04:30.167 --> 00:04:32.200
-A decade.
-I really do.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:34.467
Does it change the music?

00:04:34.467 --> 00:04:35.868
Does it change the album
and the tour?

00:04:35.868 --> 00:04:37.234
And you're like, "Oh, wait.

00:04:37.234 --> 00:04:38.834
Maybe I should go back
and re-record that?"

00:04:38.834 --> 00:04:41.033
-You know, I think that it
creates some moments

00:04:41.033 --> 00:04:45.300
of introspection of, again,
"Who am I?"

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:46.601
That's kind of --

00:04:46.601 --> 00:04:48.701
The stripping away
is the part of the process

00:04:48.701 --> 00:04:49.868
of writing an album.

00:04:49.868 --> 00:04:52.934
It's not adding more to,
but peeling back layers.

00:04:52.934 --> 00:04:55.000
Uncovering the veil.
Getting to the heart.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:57.467
And the relapse
was an opportunity for me

00:04:57.467 --> 00:04:59.801
to get back to the place of,
"Okay. What went on?

00:04:59.801 --> 00:05:01.701
Let me talk about it.
Let's get vulnerable.

00:05:01.701 --> 00:05:04.601
And what are you
afraid to say right now?"

00:05:04.601 --> 00:05:06.200
That's what
you need to lean into.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:09.167
-Congratulations on the album
and getting everything.

00:05:09.167 --> 00:05:10.434
-Thank you.
-We love you so much.

00:05:10.434 --> 00:05:11.634
-Thank you.
-Give it up for Macklemore

00:05:11.634 --> 00:05:13.734
right there, guys.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:13.734 --> 00:05:15.701
Congrats.
The new album, "Ben,"

00:05:15.701 --> 00:05:17.234
comes out this Friday,

00:05:17.234 --> 00:05:18.934
and you're gonna be back
on our show next week.

00:05:18.934 --> 00:05:20.534
-Yes.
-So, yeah, so come right back.

00:05:20.534 --> 00:05:22.234
Don't leave.
Macklemore, everybody.

00:05:22.234 --> 00:05:24.300
More "Tonight Show."
Stick around. Come on back.

